\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell provided an update on last weekend\rquote s Free Paper Shredding Event at Mira Costa High School, reporting that 6.15 tons of documents were securely shredded and recycled. He also announced that the final Free Paper Shredding Event of the year will take place on October 18, 2025.\line\line Police Chief Rachel Johnson invited the community to attend the upcoming \ldblquote Cones With a Cop\rdblquote  event at Handel\rquote s Ice Cream on August 13, 2025, from 3:00 PM to 5:00 PM.\line\line Los Angeles County Library West Regional Administrator Don Rowe introduced Cassandra Sargent as the new Manager of the Manhattan Beach Library.\line\line Library Manager Cassandra Sargent invited the community to several upcoming events at the Manhattan Beach Library: the Summer Discovery Wrap-Up Party on August 7, 2025, from 11:00 AM to 12:00 PM; \ldblquote Anime Your Way,\rdblquote  a step-by-step anime drawing workshop on August 14, 2025, from 3:00 PM to 4:00 PM; and a cello performance by Chelsea Wong on August 30, 2025, from 2:00 PM to 3:00 PM.\line\line Beach Cities Health District Boardmember Jane Diehl announced the upcoming Purpose Workshop and Social Connection Fair, taking place at the Redondo Beach Center for Spiritual Living on August 16, 2025, from 1:30 PM to 3:30 PM.\cf1\i0\f1\par
}


